On-device AI refers to using pre-trained AI models trained on specific data, like images or text, that are already on the device. Instead of training the AI model on the data itself, it works with the data that's already available. This means the AI model can perform tasks like image recognition or sentiment analysis directly on the data the user has on their device, without needing to download or store the model.

